    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 34 tests pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 including the new `Cp23Tests` (GOLD), `Cp15Tests` (SILVER/BRONZE), and the household tests `Cp10`/`Cp11`/`Cp13`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier following the existing `namesakeCount` snapshot pattern in this codebase. Membership tier is derived at serialization time by `OwnerMapper` from a single `Owner`, so \u2014 like `namesakeCount` \u2014 the household size is computed and persisted at create time.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`OwnerMapper.membershipTier(...)`** \u2014 GOLD now takes precedence: returns `GOLD` when the owner's persisted `householdMemberCount >= 3`; otherwise the existing SILVER (namesakeCount 0 + email) / BRONZE rules apply unchanged.\n\n2. **New pipeline step `AssignHouseholdMemberCount`** \u2014 runs after `AssignHouseholdId` (so `householdId` is set) and before `SaveOwner`, within the same write transaction. It counts already-persisted owners sharing this owner's `householdId` and adds 1 for the not-yet-saved new owner, giving the household size *after this create*. Wired into `owners.POST.yml` between `assignHouseholdId` and `assignNamesakeCount`.\n\n3. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added the persisted `householdMemberCount` field (`household_member_count` column) with getter/setter, plus a `@Mapping(ignore = true)` on the inbound `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` mapping (it's a derived, read-only value).\n\n4. **Schema** \u2014 added `household_member_count INTEGER` to all four dialects (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres). Seed `data.sql` inserts all use explicit column lists, so the nullable column is safe.\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum (regenerating `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum` at build) and updated its description.\n\nThe snapshot semantics match the spec's \"after this create\" wording and mirror how `namesakeCount` already works: each owner's tier reflects the household size at its own creation time.",
